<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Igbomina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Igbomina are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> subgroup living in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorubaland">Yorubaland</a>, mostly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwara-state">Kwara State</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osun-state">Osun State</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, with towns such as Ila-Orangun and Omu-Aran. In the 19th century they were caught between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilorin">Ilorin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibadan">Ibadan</a>, and some of their towns joined the Ekiti Parapo alliance in the Kiriji War against Ibadan.</p></div>
